1. The run's abort signal reaches every Mistral request: the raw stream
   fetch and structuredOutput's chat.complete (ai-mistral 0.6.11 main has
   neither). Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
2. A non-OK response's error carries its HTTP status and parsed body, and the
   RUN_ERROR forwards them as rawEvent, as the SDK-based adapters do since
   TanStack/ai#985. The rethrow after RUN_ERROR is upstream's (tested) and
   stays. Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
3. finish_reason model_length reads as length, and finish_reason error ends
   the run in a RUN_ERROR (code incomplete-stream, as TanStack/ai#1494 names
   a cut-off stream) instead of a finished answer. Upstream PR to be opened;
   remove when released.

